"3019","On the authority of ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: Sawdah went out after the verse of hijāb was revealed, to attend to her need. She was a large woman who could not go unrecognized by anyone who knew her. ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb saw her and said: “O Sawdah! By Allah, you cannot hide from us, so consider how you go out.” She said: So she turned back, returning. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was in my house, dining, and in his hand was a bone (with meat on it). She entered and said: “O Messenger of Allah! I went out for some need of mine, and ʿUmar said to me such and such.” She said: Then Allah sent revelation to him, then the revelation was lifted from him, while the bone was still in his hand—he had not put it down. He said: “Indeed, permission has been given to you to go out for your needs.” And in a narration: “for your needs (plural).”"
